1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:09,000
Welcome to GameGear Signature Edition,
a precision-focused gaming accessories storefront developed for the Fynd Hiring Hackathon.

2
00:00:09,200 --> 00:00:20,000
GameGear presents two synthetic gaming products:
the Arc M1 Gaming Mouse at ₹1,499, and the Forge TKL Mechanical Keyboard at ₹3,499.

3
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:33,000
Each product features custom technical vector artwork and an interactive inspection modal
with three distinct views: isometric 3/4, top plan, and macro component details.

4
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:46,000
The shopping experience includes dynamic cart management, real-time quantity adjustments,
and zero-floating-point financial calculations performed strictly in integer rupees.

5
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:58,000
Customers can inspect their order ledger, review unit totals,
and proceed through a validated checkout protected by a synchronous double-submission lock.

6
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:12,000
The application rigorously prevents empty-cart checkout and rejects blank customer names.
Placing an order generates a unique reference and a printable digital receipt.

7
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:26,000
Behind the storefront is a comprehensive browser automation harness built with Python,
pytest, and Playwright, featuring 21 passing automated tests with zero flaky steps.

8
00:01:26,200 --> 00:01:38,000
The suite verifies mandatory user journeys, regression edge cases, accessibility standards,
theme persistence, and multi-viewport responsiveness with genuine screenshot evidence.

9
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:48,000
GameGear is a pure client-side prototype using synthetic demonstration data.
The complete source code, test plan, and execution reports are published openly on GitHub.

10
00:01:48,200 --> 00:01:56,000
GameGear Signature Edition.
Designed for control. Engineered for confidence.
